msgid "Enable"
msgstr ""

msgid "Starts the agent, enables it at boot, and opens TCP 8090 plus UDP 29820/29821 on the WAN zone, so an AC on the upstream or LAN side can discover and manage this access point during initial setup. On by default."
msgstr ""

msgid "Controller address"
msgstr ""

msgid "host:port of the controller, for example 10.0.30.5:8090. Leave empty to find the controller by UDP broadcast on the local segment; a controller on the other side of a router must be entered explicitly, because broadcast never crosses layer 3."
msgstr ""

msgid "Shared secret"
msgstr ""

msgid "Must match AC_SHARED_SECRET on the controller. Leave empty when the controller does not check one."
msgstr ""

msgid "Heartbeat interval"
msgstr ""

msgid "Seconds between two polls. The default is 20."
msgstr ""

msgid "Dry run"
msgstr ""

msgid "Render and stage the configuration but never write /etc/config and never reload radios. Use this to check that the controller can be reached before letting it take over."
msgstr ""

msgid "Peer coordination port"
msgstr ""

msgid "UDP port used to exchange 802.11k data between access points directly. 0 disables it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Peer announcement interval"
msgstr ""

msgid "How often this access point announces its BSS and client state to its peers, for example 30s."
msgstr ""

msgid "Local roam suggestion"
msgstr ""

msgid "Let the agent itself send one 802.11v transition suggestion (BTM) when a client is very weak and a peer serves the same SSID. This is built into the agent and needs no steering daemon. It stays silent whenever a steering daemon (usteer or dawn) is enabled, so two decision-makers never fight over the same client; nrsyncd only distributes 11k neighbour lists and does not compete."
msgstr ""

msgid "Settings saved. The agent and the WAN rules now follow the switch."
msgstr ""

msgid "Settings saved. The agent restarts to pick them up."
msgstr ""

msgid "Could not save the settings: %s"
msgstr ""

msgid "Save & apply"
msgstr ""

msgid "Reset"
msgstr ""

msgid "The controller no longer knows this access point, but rev %d is still running here. Adopt it again to resume management."
msgstr ""

msgid "Roaming steering policy"
msgstr ""

msgid "Decides who runs client steering. While the controller answers, its directive always wins: the daemon it names is enabled and dawn/usteer are stopped, so the two never fight over a client. \"Controller first\" additionally hands steering to a local daemon when the controller is lost."
msgstr ""

msgid "Controller first (recommended)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Controller only, keep last state on loss"
msgstr ""

msgid "Autonomous: local daemons only"
msgstr ""

msgid "Steering fallback on controller loss"
msgstr ""

msgid "Which local daemon takes over after the controller has been unreachable for about a minute. Steering returns to the controller automatically once it answers again. Only used with the \"Controller first\" policy; \"none\" keeps the last controller state instead."
msgstr ""

